WEBVTT

00:22.021 --> 00:23.857
Oh, there you are!

00:23.940 --> 00:24.858
What?

00:26.901 --> 00:29.070
Jogo!

00:34.617 --> 00:36.995
Seems like your body
is almost completely restored.

00:37.495 --> 00:40.498
Yes, it's comfortable to live here.

00:40.582 --> 00:42.917
No humans can come close.

00:43.001 --> 00:45.879
I guess it's really inconvenient
when you don't have a body.

00:45.962 --> 00:48.631
Self-regeneration
is really inefficient, too.

00:48.715 --> 00:49.883
Mahito.

00:49.966 --> 00:53.178
Seems like you used up
a lot of cursed energy as well.

00:53.261 --> 00:55.138
Oh, you can tell?

00:55.221 --> 00:58.892
Ryomen Sukuna and his vessel
are my nemesis.

00:59.851 --> 01:03.980
This game started when I met my new toy,

01:04.481 --> 01:06.816
but it didn't go well.

01:06.900 --> 01:08.359
It wasn't bad at first, though.

01:08.860 --> 01:13.406
I should have taken the toy hostage,
and forced Itadori to make a Binding Vow.

01:13.490 --> 01:18.119
If you don't want him to die,
hand over your body to Sukuna.

01:19.746 --> 01:24.125
No, a Binding Vow
can only be done by himself.

01:24.209 --> 01:28.505
It's not that simple to initiate
a Binding Vow through intervention.

01:30.715 --> 01:32.884
Maybe it would have been better

01:32.967 --> 01:35.762
if I just gave him a fatal blow
instead of transfiguring him.

01:36.429 --> 01:39.557
Maybe Sukuna could have treated him
with his Reverse Cursed Technique.

01:41.309 --> 01:44.896
Know your place, you fool.

01:46.022 --> 01:50.777
No, that's how he is.
He'll refuse no matter what.

01:52.070 --> 01:53.321
Jogo.

01:54.155 --> 01:56.157
After coming in contact with Sukuna,

01:56.241 --> 01:59.327
I think it's better
to follow Geto's plan first.

01:59.911 --> 02:02.705
Sukuna is worth the effort.

02:05.125 --> 02:09.879
Collect all fingers
and offer it to Sukuna?

02:10.797 --> 02:14.551
It doesn't matter
if we all die in the process.

02:15.468 --> 02:16.928
Right?

02:17.971 --> 02:19.472
Very well.

02:19.556 --> 02:23.560
It doesn't have to be me smiling
in the wilderness 100 years later.

02:23.643 --> 02:26.896
I'm fine with it,
as long as curses live as humans.

02:26.980 --> 02:29.399
Oh, you get it.

02:29.482 --> 02:34.028
So let's collect all six fingers
kept by Jujutsu High School.

02:34.112 --> 02:35.363
Is that necessary?

02:35.864 --> 02:39.617
Jujutsu Sorcerers keep Yuji Itadori
because they want him

02:39.701 --> 02:41.369
to swallow Sukuna's fingers, right?

02:41.452 --> 02:43.663
Even if we ignore him,
he'll eat it by himself.

02:44.247 --> 02:45.623
The higher-ups of Jujutsu High

02:45.707 --> 02:49.627
still can't judge
Yuji Itadori's strength as a vessel.

02:49.711 --> 02:52.714
They don't know how many fingers it takes
for him to lose control.

02:52.797 --> 02:56.551
They will probably gather all the fingers
before making him swallow all at once.

02:57.427 --> 02:59.596
Although there's one exception.

03:00.096 --> 03:02.682
I want him to eat it quickly!

03:02.765 --> 03:04.976
We can't wait that long, right?

03:05.059 --> 03:09.397
In a worst-case scenario,
the higher-ups might kill Yuji Itadori.

03:09.898 --> 03:12.442
Nothing ventured, nothing gained.

03:12.984 --> 03:15.111
What should we do?

03:15.194 --> 03:16.863
I've made the arrangements.

03:17.363 --> 03:21.868
That's why I let Jujutsu High School
gather the fingers I collected.

04:59.966 --> 05:05.471
Nanami, tell me something interesting.

05:06.931 --> 05:08.808
All right, I got it!

05:08.891 --> 05:12.353
Let's play catch with scrap rice balls

05:12.437 --> 05:14.564
and discuss secularism!

05:14.647 --> 05:17.108
Then I'll upload a video on it.
It will be so popular!

05:18.860 --> 05:20.570
Go and have fun on your own.

05:21.070 --> 05:22.822
What kind of idea is that?

05:24.324 --> 05:29.037
Let's play Yamanote Line game
at Satoru Gojo's favorite location!

05:29.620 --> 05:31.039
All

05:32.081 --> 05:34.500
Please keep it up.

05:34.584 --> 05:39.047
Itadori needs your stupidity now.

05:40.757 --> 05:43.593
I'll let you complete a few big missions.

05:44.927 --> 05:48.848
That wasn't what I meant
when I said "big."

05:49.432 --> 05:50.558
Nanami.

05:50.641 --> 05:53.186
Did you tell Yuji about
the finger in Yoshino's house--

05:53.269 --> 05:54.729
I didn't tell him.

05:54.812 --> 05:58.149
He will probably
blame himself unnecessarily.

05:58.816 --> 06:00.860
I'm glad I left this up to you.

06:00.943 --> 06:02.653
So where's the finger?

06:03.946 --> 06:06.324
I've handed it over to the superiors.

06:06.407 --> 06:09.952
If I give it to you,
you'll let Itadori eat it, right?

06:10.578 --> 06:14.665
But are you really letting him
return to the team?

06:15.166 --> 06:17.877
If you announce it at the Goodwill Event,

06:17.960 --> 06:20.379
he'll be targeted by the higher-ups again.

06:20.463 --> 06:23.174
Even so, I believe Yuji will be fine.

06:23.257 --> 06:26.052
You should know it well.

06:27.053 --> 06:28.346
What?

06:28.429 --> 06:30.056
Mr. Gojo!

06:31.724 --> 06:33.476
Nanami is here too.

06:33.559 --> 06:34.477
Hey!

06:34.560 --> 06:36.979
Let's go meet them now.

06:37.063 --> 06:38.523
I'm excited!

06:38.606 --> 06:39.774
I'm excited!

06:39.857 --> 06:42.026
I'm excited!

06:42.110 --> 06:43.194
Yuji.

06:43.277 --> 06:44.403
Don't tell me that

06:44.487 --> 06:47.657
you've been hiding for so long,
and now you want to appear normally?

06:47.740 --> 06:49.200
Can't I?

06:49.992 --> 06:52.161
For a dead friend
to reappear after two months

06:52.245 --> 06:54.038
saying they were alive…

06:54.122 --> 06:56.290
Even Jujutsu Sorcerers
don't get that often.

06:56.374 --> 06:58.251
You should give them a surprise.

07:00.711 --> 07:02.588
In short, just leave it to me.

07:02.672 --> 07:03.631
What?

07:06.634 --> 07:09.720
The first-year students will be
shocked, happy, crying, and laughing.

07:09.804 --> 07:12.223
The second-year
and Kyoto's students will cry as well.

07:12.306 --> 07:15.268
Some will cry until they vomit!

07:16.352 --> 07:19.689
They will cry so much that
even global warming will be resolved!

07:22.692 --> 07:23.943
Nice!

07:24.026 --> 07:25.278
What should I do?

07:25.361 --> 07:27.447
Mr. Gojo, what should I do?

07:27.530 --> 07:29.073
You don't have to do anything.

07:29.157 --> 07:30.950
Just do as I say.

07:31.033 --> 07:32.535
Just go along with my plan.

07:32.618 --> 07:34.454
So what should I do to follow your plan?

07:34.537 --> 07:37.707
-You being alive is already a surprise.
-Just flow along with me.

07:37.790 --> 07:38.916
Why…

07:39.500 --> 07:41.919
Why is everyone all empty-handed?

07:42.003 --> 07:43.087
-What?
-What?

07:43.171 --> 07:45.423
That's our question.
What's with all the luggage?

07:45.506 --> 07:48.426
I mean we're going to Kyoto, right?

07:48.509 --> 07:51.929
The Sister-School Goodwill Event in Kyoto.

07:52.013 --> 07:55.266
It's a Sister-School Goodwill Event
with the Kyoto School…

07:55.349 --> 07:56.309
held in Tokyo.

07:56.392 --> 07:57.435
FAMOUS IN UENO
PANDA

07:57.518 --> 07:59.896
No way!

07:59.979 --> 08:03.065
-No wonder I've always felt weird.
-What am I preparing for?

08:03.149 --> 08:04.859
-Yes.
-Salmon.

08:04.942 --> 08:07.904
-It's held by last year's winner.
-This is too much! It's a fraud!

08:07.987 --> 08:09.947
Don't go winning, idiot!

08:10.031 --> 08:12.241
We didn't compete last year!

08:12.325 --> 08:15.453
Yuta was the only one who joined
last year to make up for the numbers.

08:15.536 --> 08:17.413
That was before Rika was freed.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.540
I heard that he dominated the competition.

08:19.624 --> 08:21.751
But it was held in Kyoto,
so we didn't see it.

08:22.502 --> 08:25.046
I won't forgive you, Yuta Okkotsu!

08:25.129 --> 08:27.632
Although I've never met you before!

08:27.715 --> 08:29.091
That's unjustified resentment.

08:29.175 --> 08:30.426
-Salmon.
-What?

08:33.513 --> 08:36.432
Hey. They are here.

08:37.266 --> 08:38.392
Oh, my.

08:38.476 --> 08:41.562
Everyone from the Tokyo school is here.

08:43.439 --> 08:45.274
Are you here to greet us?

08:45.983 --> 08:47.276
It's really disgusting.

08:47.360 --> 08:49.278
MAI ZENIN
SECOND-YEAR STUDENT

08:49.362 --> 08:51.781
Okkotsu is not here.

08:51.864 --> 08:53.783
AOI TODO
THIRD-YEAR STUDENT

08:53.866 --> 08:56.744
Shut up and give me those boxes of cakes.

08:56.827 --> 08:59.080
Yatsuhashi, kuzukiri,
and buckwheat biscuits, too!

08:59.163 --> 09:00.122
Salmon.

09:00.206 --> 09:01.791
Are you guys hungry?

09:01.874 --> 09:03.834
What's wrong with that first-year student?

09:03.918 --> 09:04.794
It's terrifying.

09:04.877 --> 09:06.796
MOMO NISHIMIYA
THIRD-YEAR STUDENT

09:06.879 --> 09:09.006
It's good that Okkotsu is not here,

09:09.090 --> 09:11.133
but two first-years
is too much of a handicap.

09:11.217 --> 09:12.301
It's a robot!

09:12.385 --> 09:14.303
ULTIMATE MECHAMARU
SECOND-YEAR STUDENT

09:14.387 --> 09:17.306
A Jujutsu Sorcerer's strength
has nothing to do with age.

09:17.390 --> 09:19.308
NORITOSHI KAMO
THIRD-YEAR STUDENT

09:19.392 --> 09:21.310
Especially Fushiguro.

09:21.894 --> 09:24.313
He's from the bloodline
of the Zenin Family.

09:24.397 --> 09:26.774
He's much better
than the main family bloodline.

09:26.857 --> 09:27.775
Damn it.

09:27.858 --> 09:28.943
What's wrong?

09:29.026 --> 09:30.027
Nothing.

09:30.111 --> 09:31.237
Hey there, you guys.

09:31.320 --> 09:33.155
You two should calm down.

09:33.239 --> 09:35.157
KASUMI MIWA
SECOND-YEAR STUDENT

09:35.992 --> 09:39.078
Come on. Don't quarrel among ourselves.

09:39.161 --> 09:41.539
You kids…

09:41.622 --> 09:43.541
UTAHIME IORI
SEMI-GRADE 1 JUJUTSU SORCERER

09:43.624 --> 09:46.043
So where's that fool?

09:46.127 --> 09:47.670
Satoru is late.

09:47.753 --> 09:50.464
There's no way a fool
is going to be on time.

09:50.548 --> 09:53.509
Nobody said that fool is Mr. Gojo.

09:53.593 --> 09:54.552
-What?
-What?

09:57.597 --> 09:59.473
Sorry to keep you waiting!

09:59.557 --> 10:00.433
Damn it.

10:00.516 --> 10:01.976
-Satoru Gojo.
-Satoru Gojo!

10:02.935 --> 10:05.313
Hey, everyone's here!

10:05.396 --> 10:08.357
I went on a business trip abroad.

10:08.441 --> 10:10.943
So I brought some souvenirs for everyone.

10:11.027 --> 10:12.361
That's sudden.

10:12.445 --> 10:13.946
Isn't it because of his jet lag?

10:14.030 --> 10:15.948
-Here's for everyone from Kyoto.
-What?

10:16.032 --> 10:17.700
An amulet of a certain tribe.

10:17.783 --> 10:19.035
None for Utahime.

10:19.118 --> 10:20.202
I don't want it!

10:20.286 --> 10:23.331
And this is a local product
for everyone from Tokyo!

10:25.416 --> 10:27.710
Overly-excited adults are creepy.

10:31.255 --> 10:34.216
Yes! OPP!

10:34.300 --> 10:37.011
This is Yuji Itadori,
who was presumed dead!

10:40.640 --> 10:42.016
What?

10:42.099 --> 10:43.142
What?

10:43.225 --> 10:44.518
What?

10:44.602 --> 10:47.480
They don't look happy at all!

10:48.356 --> 10:49.607
No way…

10:49.690 --> 10:51.776
Hello, everyone from Kyoto.

10:51.859 --> 10:55.112
This is Ryomen Sukuna's vessel,
Yuji Itadori.

10:55.196 --> 10:56.489
The Kyoto students…

10:57.323 --> 11:00.076
They are only interested in the dolls!

11:01.869 --> 11:04.205
Sukuna's vessel?

11:04.288 --> 11:06.499
What's going on?

11:06.582 --> 11:08.501
YOSHINOBU GAKUGANJI
PRINCIPAL

11:08.584 --> 11:09.502
What?

11:09.585 --> 11:11.504
Principal Gakuganji!

11:11.587 --> 11:14.507
My, I'm so glad!

11:14.590 --> 11:19.845
I was worried that
you were going to die from shock.

11:21.097 --> 11:23.015
Curse you, brat!

11:28.562 --> 11:29.397
Hey.

11:29.480 --> 11:30.773
Yes?

11:30.856 --> 11:32.983
There's something you should say, right?

11:33.067 --> 11:33.901
What?

11:37.988 --> 11:43.077
I'm sorry for not telling you
that I'm still alive.

11:43.160 --> 11:45.955
ITADORI JOINS THE FRAY

11:56.048 --> 12:00.010
TOKYO-KYOTO
SISTER-SCHOOL GOODWILL EVENT

12:00.094 --> 12:02.555
The Tokyo-Kyoto
Sister-School Goodwill Event

12:02.638 --> 12:05.349
will be held across two days.

12:05.433 --> 12:08.227
First day, we'll have a team battle.

12:09.270 --> 12:10.980
WACKY SPIRIT BASH RACE

12:11.063 --> 12:14.567
It's the Wacky Spirit Bash Race!

12:16.569 --> 12:18.320
The rules are simple.

12:18.863 --> 12:22.116
The team who eliminates
the Grade 2 Cursed Spirit

12:22.199 --> 12:25.077
released within the school grounds wins!

12:25.661 --> 12:29.206
Grade 3 and below Cursed Spirits
have been released, too.

12:29.290 --> 12:31.834
If there's no winner before sunset,

12:31.917 --> 12:35.463
the winner is decided
by the number of eliminations.

12:35.546 --> 12:37.965
There are no other rules.

12:38.048 --> 12:41.427
You may hinder your opponents in the race,

12:41.510 --> 12:45.514
but don't forget that you are comrades
in the fight against the curses.

12:45.598 --> 12:48.601
The Goodwill Event
is for you to understand

12:48.684 --> 12:50.978
your comrades and yourself
in the competition.

12:51.687 --> 12:53.355
Please don't kill each other.

12:53.439 --> 12:57.568
Don't cause irreparable damage
to your opponent.

12:59.320 --> 13:02.615
All right, you are all dismissed.

13:02.698 --> 13:03.991
The race will begin at noon!

13:06.869 --> 13:08.412
TOKYO SCHOOL TEAM MEETING

13:08.496 --> 13:10.080
Excuse me.

13:10.164 --> 13:13.000
We're comrades.

13:13.083 --> 13:15.920
This kind of bullying
seems a bit excessive.

13:16.003 --> 13:18.130
Shut up.
Keep it like that for the time being.

13:18.214 --> 13:19.381
Come on, now.

13:19.465 --> 13:23.135
He has explained the reason.
Just forgive him.

13:23.219 --> 13:24.845
The panda spoke!

13:24.929 --> 13:26.430
Salmon.

13:26.514 --> 13:27.806
What?

13:27.890 --> 13:30.434
Inumaki is
a Cursed Speech Jujutsu Sorcerer.

13:30.518 --> 13:34.271
His cursed technique enhances and
forcefully activates the effects of words.

13:34.355 --> 13:37.358
He limits his vocabulary
for safety purposes.

13:37.441 --> 13:40.277
If you tell someone to die,
will that person really die?

13:40.361 --> 13:41.570
Impressive.

13:41.654 --> 13:43.989
It's not as convenient as you think.

13:44.073 --> 13:47.034
It depends on
the strength of the sorcerer.

13:47.117 --> 13:50.412
Using strong vocabulary
will get a strong rebound,

13:50.496 --> 13:52.831
and it rebounds to himself at worst.

13:53.332 --> 13:57.086
So the vocabulary restriction
is also to protect himself.

13:57.169 --> 13:58.504
I see.

13:58.587 --> 14:01.298
So why can you talk?

14:01.382 --> 14:02.716
Are you a new breed of panda?

14:02.800 --> 14:05.135
How could he reveal
someone else's cursed technique?

14:05.219 --> 14:06.220
It's okay.

14:06.303 --> 14:08.472
It won't matter
if Toge's technique is revealed.

14:08.973 --> 14:11.600
-Anyway, Yuji…
-What?

14:11.684 --> 14:13.602
Give me back the Slaughter Demon.

14:14.353 --> 14:15.896
Satoru lent it to you, right?

14:17.898 --> 14:19.942
Well…

14:21.944 --> 14:23.279
Lend me.

14:23.779 --> 14:24.989
Here you go.

14:26.615 --> 14:28.534
I broke it.

14:28.617 --> 14:30.244
Give it back.

14:32.413 --> 14:35.749
It's with Mr. Gojo.

14:35.833 --> 14:38.419
That stupid blindfolded man!

14:38.502 --> 14:39.837
Really?

14:43.257 --> 14:44.258
That's disgusting.

14:44.341 --> 14:46.552
So what's the plan?

14:46.635 --> 14:49.763
We expected a team battle,

14:49.847 --> 14:51.682
but our members have increased.

14:51.765 --> 14:53.976
Changing our battle strategy?
There's no time.

14:54.059 --> 14:55.185
Bonito flakes.

14:55.269 --> 14:58.188
That depends on Yuji. What can you do?

14:58.689 --> 15:00.024
I can punch and kick.

15:00.107 --> 15:03.986
-There are enough people who can do that.
-What?

15:04.945 --> 15:08.532
I don't know what this guy
did while he was dead,

15:09.116 --> 15:10.868
but if Tokyo and Kyoto School students

15:10.951 --> 15:13.662
fight without cursed energy…

15:14.246 --> 15:16.206
Itadori will win.

15:16.290 --> 15:17.750
Wow.

15:18.751 --> 15:21.545
Megumi has fought Aoi before,

15:22.338 --> 15:24.173
so he's credible.

15:24.757 --> 15:26.383
Interesting.

15:30.054 --> 15:31.221
KYOTO SCHOOL TEAM MEETING

15:31.305 --> 15:33.432
Sukuna's vessel…

15:33.933 --> 15:36.769
Kill Yuji Itadori.

15:36.852 --> 15:38.854
That is not a human.

15:38.938 --> 15:41.190
You can do whatever.

15:41.273 --> 15:43.150
I'll treat it as an accident.

15:43.233 --> 15:45.861
No need to worry or hesitate.

15:45.945 --> 15:47.863
How unpleasant.

15:47.947 --> 15:49.949
Regardless of whether
we can kill him or not,

15:50.032 --> 15:52.868
he's here because he can't die, right?

15:52.952 --> 15:56.872
I heard that he committed suicide.

15:56.956 --> 16:01.835
What do you need to pay attention to
when killing a Jujutsu Sorcerer?

16:01.919 --> 16:02.962
Kamo.

16:03.045 --> 16:03.879
Yes.

16:04.463 --> 16:07.299
To prevent Jujutsu Sorcerers
from becoming curses after death,

16:07.383 --> 16:08.884
we kill them with cursed energy.

16:08.968 --> 16:10.344
That's right.

16:10.427 --> 16:14.932
There will be no problem
if you kill him with cursed energy.

16:15.015 --> 16:18.894
Now Yuji Itadori
has control over the body.

16:18.978 --> 16:22.272
As long as Sukuna doesn't appear,
he's just a normal first-year student.

16:22.356 --> 16:23.857
It's easy to kill--

16:25.442 --> 16:27.528
Lame. Do as you like.

16:27.611 --> 16:29.029
Todo, come back.

16:29.738 --> 16:32.032
The principal is not finished yet.

16:32.116 --> 16:36.704
Takada will make a guest appearance
on the 11:00 a.m. walking show.

16:36.787 --> 16:39.039
Do I need to explain further?

16:39.123 --> 16:41.917
Just record the show. Come back.

16:42.001 --> 16:45.045
I want to watch both the premiere
and the recording!

16:45.546 --> 16:47.297
Are you looking down on me?

16:49.633 --> 16:50.884
That's not the point.

16:50.968 --> 16:52.678
Listen carefully.

16:52.761 --> 16:54.596
You too, old man!

16:54.680 --> 16:59.601
I've long been disappointed
in everyone's poor taste in women.

16:59.685 --> 17:02.604
Just use whatever strategy you want.

17:02.688 --> 17:06.108
However, try giving me another order…

17:06.191 --> 17:07.693
I'll kill you.

17:11.822 --> 17:13.323
What should we do?

17:13.407 --> 17:17.327
It seems that he's not going to
participate in our battle strategy.

17:17.411 --> 17:19.705
The principal is gone too.

17:19.788 --> 17:22.791
To be honest,
I don't want to be killed by him.

17:22.875 --> 17:24.835
It should be okay.

17:24.918 --> 17:28.714
That guy's going to fight
the Tokyo guys either way.

17:28.797 --> 17:30.883
Since he wants to go rampant,

17:30.966 --> 17:33.761
we just need to focus on the game.

17:33.844 --> 17:37.723
But we have to kill Yuji Itadori.

17:37.806 --> 17:39.475
Are we really killing him?

17:39.975 --> 17:43.353
I don't think he's going to kill him.

17:43.437 --> 17:45.189
Although it looks like he might.

17:45.272 --> 17:47.900
Then we have to keep an eye on Todo,

17:47.983 --> 17:51.779
and deal a fatal blow to Yuji Itadori.

17:51.862 --> 17:53.572
I don't want to do it.

17:54.198 --> 17:57.242
Since we have to deal
with Cursed Spirits too,

17:57.326 --> 17:58.994
I think two on one is just right.

17:59.495 --> 18:00.621
No.

18:00.704 --> 18:03.582
Among the Jujutsu Sorcerers
of Jujutsu High School,

18:03.665 --> 18:07.211
the appearance of a half-baked person
like Yuji Itadori is extremely serious.

18:07.711 --> 18:09.630
Regardless of the Goodwill Event,

18:10.214 --> 18:12.758
I can't turn a blind eye
as a member of Kamo Family.

18:13.717 --> 18:17.971
Everyone from Kyoto School
will attack Yuji Itadori.

18:18.597 --> 18:19.598
Wait a minute.

18:19.681 --> 18:23.560
What if Itadori and Inumaki are together?

18:24.144 --> 18:26.814
It's too risky for us
since his Cursed Speech

18:26.897 --> 18:28.482
can take us all out at once.

18:28.565 --> 18:31.443
At worst, we might get wiped out.

18:32.152 --> 18:34.071
She's right.

18:34.571 --> 18:39.076
No, it's not that scary
since we know his technique.

18:39.159 --> 18:41.286
I'll take care of Maki.

18:41.370 --> 18:43.580
Give me that brown-haired
first-year student too.

18:43.664 --> 18:45.165
Listen to what you say.

18:45.249 --> 18:47.167
You're acting like Todo.

18:49.837 --> 18:52.464
So what do you want to talk about?

18:53.048 --> 18:54.883
What? Why are you angry?

18:55.467 --> 18:57.386
I'm not angry.

18:57.469 --> 19:00.931
That's right. I didn't do anything.

19:01.974 --> 19:04.059
Someone in Jujutsu High School…

19:04.643 --> 19:07.396
is colluding with
Cursed Users or Cursed Spirits.

19:08.397 --> 19:09.731
Impossible!

19:09.815 --> 19:12.192
I can understand Cursed Users,
but Cursed Spirits?

19:12.276 --> 19:16.238
Recently, Cursed Spirits
of that level keep emerging.

19:16.321 --> 19:20.284
They not only understand words,
but can even act in a group.

19:20.367 --> 19:21.994
That person may think

19:22.077 --> 19:24.329
they are just colluding with Cursed Users.

19:24.955 --> 19:28.292
So I want you to help me
investigate the Kyoto campus.

19:29.376 --> 19:32.296
What if I'm the mole?

19:32.379 --> 19:33.797
That's impossible.

19:33.881 --> 19:36.425
You're weak, and you don't have the guts--

19:38.969 --> 19:40.220
You're terrifying.

19:40.304 --> 19:44.391
-No man likes a fierce woman!
-I'm your senior!

19:48.937 --> 19:49.897
Itadori.

19:49.980 --> 19:50.814
What?

19:51.398 --> 19:52.441
Are you okay?

19:52.524 --> 19:53.400
Yes.

19:53.483 --> 19:56.236
Seems like I've got a big role,
but there'll always be a way.

19:56.320 --> 19:57.905
I'm not talking about that.

19:57.988 --> 19:59.239
Something happened, right?

19:59.990 --> 20:01.241
Nothing happened.

20:04.536 --> 20:05.746
Something did happen.

20:07.289 --> 20:10.459
But I'm really fine.

20:11.335 --> 20:15.214
In fact, I don't want to lose
because of that.

20:16.340 --> 20:17.716
Good.

20:18.300 --> 20:21.136
I kind of don't want to lose, either.

20:21.220 --> 20:23.013
What do you mean "kind of"?

20:23.096 --> 20:25.057
You were knocked out before.

20:25.140 --> 20:27.768
It will be a complete victory!
Let's beat them up!

20:27.851 --> 20:29.228
For Maki's sake, too!

20:29.311 --> 20:30.687
Don't say that.

20:30.771 --> 20:32.022
Spicy cod roe!

20:32.105 --> 20:34.233
Yes, for the sake of Maki!

20:34.316 --> 20:36.068
I said, stop it!

20:38.445 --> 20:39.780
Well then…

20:40.405 --> 20:41.740
To victory!

20:43.033 --> 20:44.868
Why are you taking charge?

20:44.952 --> 20:45.953
What?

22:16.752 --> 22:18.503
Juju Stroll!

22:18.587 --> 22:21.548
SUSHI EISHU

22:22.090 --> 22:23.050
All right!

22:23.133 --> 22:27.554
Today, we're here at Sushi Eishu.

22:27.637 --> 22:30.140
Why don't you try acting like her?

22:30.223 --> 22:33.018
I would, but you would scold me!

22:34.519 --> 22:36.021
Welcome.

22:48.617 --> 22:51.369
What do you like, Takada?

22:51.453 --> 22:53.163
I like blood clams.

22:53.246 --> 22:56.583
It's a perfect match
with room temperature sake!

22:56.666 --> 22:57.709
How old are you again?

22:57.793 --> 22:58.835
What did you say?

23:02.881 --> 23:05.467
How many years
have you been in this business?

23:05.967 --> 23:07.844
I started when I was 20 years old.

23:07.928 --> 23:09.596
Let me count.

23:09.679 --> 23:12.349
Did you start the business 300 years ago?

23:12.432 --> 23:13.809
Are you drunk?

23:14.392 --> 23:16.812
Thank you for waiting.
Here's your blood clam sushi.

23:21.358 --> 23:22.984
It's delicious!

23:23.068 --> 23:24.778
Can I have yours?

23:24.861 --> 23:26.321
Of course not.

23:28.615 --> 23:31.576
-I'm sorry.
-What are you thinking?

23:31.660 --> 23:34.162
-It looks really delicious.
-It's not bad.

23:34.246 --> 23:36.331
-As expected of Takada.
-This is fun!

23:36.998 --> 23:39.459
Mr. Gojo, do you know what OPP means?

23:39.543 --> 23:41.545
What? It has a meaning?

23:41.628 --> 23:45.382
-It stands for "Ocean Pacific Peace."
-Are you serious?
